Z||000000||86_Fastback||06-17-99||01:37 PM||||Well, the muffler on my 86GT is a giant rust pit.  Anyone know of a good replacement?  I am looking for a free-flowing muffler with a nice growl to it.  Of course, I will also settle for something that fits pretty easily too.<br>-Gregg
Z||000001||Bruce||06-17-99||06:11 PM||||I'm waiting for a Flowmaster that I ordered from Summit- back order was about a month. <br>My present muffler is cloae to its end, plus I wanted a freer flowing system.<br>I have an 86 GT. I was told there may be some minor modifications needed to install this new muffler, but I'll have to wait until I take the car in.
Z||000002||87GT||06-17-99||09:08 PM||||Recently, I needed to replace my whole exhaust system, so I purchased the Ocelot Exhaust system from the Fiero store.  So far, I am very happy with it.  It has a nice growl to it.8-)
Z||000003||Bruce||06-17-99||09:35 PM||||Anyone else have experience with the Ocelot exhaust?<br>I was going to replace my system with individual components that have been rated highly.
Z||000004||Pretender||06-18-99||01:05 AM||||i have the ocelot exhaust system., i HATE IT!.....but thats my opinion., it's non mandrel bent, the muffler is a cheapo poor sounding thing...the exhaust tips are nice though...but thats just my opinion...:o)
Z||000005||86_Fastback||06-18-99||05:16 AM||||Bruce,<br>Do you have the part number for that Flowmaster handy?  If it only takes minor modifications, I will go with it also.<br>
Z||000006||batboy||06-18-99||06:00 AM||||I know nothing about the Ocelot system, but a number of articles I've read puts Flowmaster near the top of the performance mufflers. I have a pair of them on a streetrod and love 'em. Fortunately, I'm on first name basis with the manager of a small local muffler shop who can custom bend and make any kind exhaust system. They do excellent work at a reasonable price. There's bound to be good shops in your area too.
Z||000007||Bruce||06-18-99||10:44 AM||||86_Fastback,<br>Thanks to this forum, the part # is: FLO 42583. I ordered mine from R&E Racing in Bakersfield, Ca. I don't have their number handy, but you can get it from the Flowmaster information links. They do not charge shipping, and have advise me weekly on the status, since it was a back-ordered item.<br>Also, try Summit @ 800-230-3030.<p>
Z||000008||Racer 1||06-18-99||10:38 PM||||Borla makes the best mufflers.They have a wide selection of muffles.Plus some real cool exhaust tips.For headers try summit racing and ask for HOOKER super competion headers for the 4 or 6 cyld fiero.Then follow up with a high flow cad-a-lackit converter.Just have your local shop custom make you a setup for you ride!
Z||000009||87FieroGT||06-18-99||10:43 PM||||I also have the Ocelot performance exhaust. The car had been hit in the rear so the tips were all meesed up. I decided to replace the whole exhaust system on the car including the cat. I don't really know if there was a performance difference, but I love the sound that it makes. I also did not use the tips that came with Ocelot system because I thought that they were ugly. Instead I went with 4" round Huge Hanna tips one on each side. It gives my Fiero a distinct look and since there are hardly any Fieros were I live it is unique.
Z||000010||SCCA FIERO||06-18-99||11:43 PM||||I put 2 4" Monza resonated tips on my V6 Fiero. I had 2 dual Hooker resonated tips on it before these and they sound the same. They are huge and I love em. Those Hondas and other cars use those 4" tips and in my opinion it sounds stupid. Those impots don't use resonated tips so they are LOUD. I was looking for something different for my Fiero. 
Z||000011||GREENDANO||06-19-99||06:14 AM||||I have the stainless steel system from IRM.  It has a very nice growl to it.  I ended up putting in a turbo tube muffler where the cat convertor was to give it an even more mellow sound.  It sounds GREAT!<br>  Dan-O
Z||000012||Pretender||06-19-99||04:46 PM||||did i read right?., hooker makes a set of headers for the 2.8?...whats the price for those things?...i hope it's alot cheaper then the fiero store.
